00:37:55.960 --> 00:37:58.490
because I think people don't feel like,

831
00:37:58.490 --> 00:38:01.750
they call it qualifying when you sit at the desk

832
00:38:01.750 --> 00:38:03.260
and tell your story, right.

833
00:38:03.260 --> 00:38:04.947
And I think a lot of people just go like,

834
00:38:04.947 --> 00:38:08.377
"No, no I don't, you know, I don't drink like that guy

835
00:38:08.377 --> 00:38:09.943
"in the gutter" or whatever.

836
00:38:12.210 --> 00:38:13.530
And that's how I felt.

837
00:38:13.530 --> 00:38:16.750
I was like, no because I'm not like, so-and-so,

838
00:38:16.750 --> 00:38:17.920
I'm like, blah, blah, blah.

839
00:38:17.920 --> 00:38:20.607
But like really when I sat in there, I was like,

840
00:38:20.607 --> 00:38:23.707
"Okay, I gotta restructure the whole way,

841
00:38:24.587 --> 00:38:29.587
"the whole way of thinking, my whole way of thinking."

842
00:38:31.068 --> 00:38:33.383
And then you don't have the thing anymore,

843
00:38:34.409 --> 00:38:36.967
you don't have the the valve, the valve's gone

844
00:38:36.967 --> 00:38:38.770
and the valve is the meetings.

845
00:38:38.770 --> 00:38:40.920
And like when you start to go (indistinct),

846
00:38:41.973 --> 00:38:43.980
you just, okay drop everything and go to a meeting

847
00:38:43.980 --> 00:38:47.210
and it'll be okay and that works.

848
00:38:47.210 --> 00:38:49.520
COVID was like, I moved to...

849
00:38:50.590 --> 00:38:52.920
I had a lot of trouble living in New York.

850
00:38:52.920 --> 00:38:54.400
I lived in New York for like...

851
00:38:54.400 --> 00:38:59.400
I moved in '98 and I'm still keeping an apartment there.

852
00:39:00.140 --> 00:39:05.140
And in my 40s, just I never lived,

853
00:39:08.400 --> 00:39:10.910
I never had enough money to like live like a New Yorker.

854
00:39:10.910 --> 00:39:13.710
Like I never made enough money, never, made enough money

855
00:39:13.710 --> 00:39:18.700
to like go to a Broadway show or take taxis.

856
00:39:18.700 --> 00:39:20.790
If I wanted to go somewhere, I had to do the subway,

857
00:39:20.790 --> 00:39:22.340
which is almost nonfunctional.

858
00:39:22.340 --> 00:39:24.760
It's the worst subway system I've ever been anywhere

859
00:39:24.760 --> 00:39:27.460
including like Lisbon, Portugal or Mexico city.

860
00:39:27.460 --> 00:39:29.460
It's the worst subway system I've ever been on.

861
00:39:29.460 --> 00:39:30.293
It's horrible.

862
00:39:30.293 --> 00:39:32.720
Highly offensive to the spirited man.

863
00:39:32.720 --> 00:39:35.870
It doesn't work, it doesn't work at all.

864
00:39:35.870 --> 00:39:40.347
And so I rode a bicycle or walked.

865
00:39:42.120 --> 00:39:46.423
So navigating around that city is very, very important.

866
00:39:47.480 --> 00:39:50.430
And there's just, this is another reason why attention

867
00:39:50.430 --> 00:39:52.900
to detail, because there's no margin for error.

868
00:39:52.900 --> 00:39:53.733
There's no margin.

869
00:39:53.733 --> 00:39:55.090
You can't leave your bike unlocked.

870
00:39:55.090 --> 00:39:58.910
Never, never, not once or else it's gonna be...

871
00:39:58.910 --> 00:40:00.323
It will be stolen.

872
00:40:01.290 --> 00:40:06.290
And that wore on me, that really wore on me

873
00:40:06.360 --> 00:40:08.100
