876
00:40:13.730 --> 00:40:15.200
and wallets and stuff.

877
00:40:15.200 --> 00:40:18.140
Thankfully New York city beat that into me

878
00:40:18.140 --> 00:40:20.790
because I think you need that degree of functionality

879
00:40:23.798 --> 00:40:24.631
to do things.

880
00:40:25.480 --> 00:40:28.240
But that stress like really, really wore on me.

881
00:40:28.240 --> 00:40:31.720
I had to go to get from my apartment to outside,

882
00:40:31.720 --> 00:40:33.780
I had to go through five doorways,

883
00:40:33.780 --> 00:40:38.570
five doorways to go from my room in my apartment to outside.

884
00:40:38.570 --> 00:40:40.940
And one of those doorways was an elevator.

885
00:40:40.940 --> 00:40:42.790
Two of those doorways were elevators.

886
00:40:46.953 --> 00:40:50.230
And being stoned, I didn't mind any of it.

887
00:40:50.230 --> 00:40:54.990
Right, so to bring it back, this is the introduction

888
00:40:54.990 --> 00:40:56.970
to drugs and alcohol as a coping mechanism

889
00:40:56.970 --> 00:40:59.410
for dealing with being flat broke in New York City

890
00:40:59.410 --> 00:41:01.320
and trying to just fucking make your way.

891
00:41:01.320 --> 00:41:05.100
Yeah, and the thing is like, I tried to get it

