00:43:25.880 --> 00:43:28.070
on a date with in New York who's like kind of a...

946
00:43:28.070 --> 00:43:30.760
She's a famous person, obviously I'm not gonna say her name.

947
00:43:30.760 --> 00:43:33.280
And it was just like, how this is so random

948
00:43:33.280 --> 00:43:34.980
but this is what this thing is.

949
00:43:34.980 --> 00:43:37.620
It's just tons of these running, the people you run into.

950
00:43:37.620 --> 00:43:40.807
Another thing about it is if I could just go on and on,

951
00:43:40.807 --> 00:43:42.900
but in my mind, it's a magical thing.

952
00:43:42.900 --> 00:43:43.900
It's something...

953
00:43:44.750 --> 00:43:47.450
I don't believe in magic, but like magic is as sort of

954
00:43:47.450 --> 00:43:49.360
an adjective we use to describe things

955
00:43:49.360 --> 00:43:51.050
that we can't explain.

956
00:43:51.050 --> 00:43:54.560
And so any kind of like people that I run into,

957
00:43:54.560 --> 00:43:55.393
that's important.

958
00:43:55.393 --> 00:43:56.988
Like if I run into someone from the past,

959
00:43:56.988 --> 00:43:58.160
that one of them, that means something,

960
00:43:58.160 --> 00:43:59.110
there's something to that.

961
00:43:59.110 --> 00:44:01.490
That's not just some random thing.

962
00:44:01.490 --> 00:44:02.541
Do you know what I mean?

963
00:44:02.541 --> 00:44:07.230
Yeah, 100%, I mean, I, I believe in the magic of AA

964
00:44:08.630 --> 00:44:11.070
like no other, I mean my life,

965
00:44:11.070 --> 00:44:13.910
it just it bears zero resemblance

966
00:44:13.910 --> 00:44:17.620
to what it was like before now.

967
00:44:17.620 --> 00:44:20.556
And it's purely a result of doing the thing

968
00:44:20.556 --> 00:44:22.807
the way that they tell you to do it.

969
00:44:22.807 --> 00:44:25.920
But the people and I think there's something really special

970
00:44:25.920 --> 00:44:28.150
about the recovery community in Los Angeles.

971
00:44:28.150 --> 00:44:30.600
The people are unbelievable.

972
00:44:30.600 --> 00:44:33.730
I've met so many incredible human beings

973
00:44:33.730 --> 00:44:35.160
that are so important to me now

974
00:44:35.160 --> 00:44:38.763
that are the most meaningful people in my life.

975
00:44:39.760 --> 00:44:43.210
And just where else, I mean, on that subject of magic,

976
00:44:43.210 --> 00:44:48.210
like just generally what other institution exists

977
00:44:51.000 --> 00:44:55.150
or you could walk into a room utterly broken, alone,

978
00:44:55.150 --> 00:45:00.150
lost, desperate, broke and be embraced by a group of people

979
00:45:01.260 --> 00:45:06.190
who truly want nothing from you other than to just help you

980
00:45:06.190 --> 00:45:07.970
and support you.

981
00:45:07.970 --> 00:45:11.250
And the only requirement is that you have a desire.

982
00:45:11.250 --> 00:45:12.550
You can go in drunk and high,

983
00:45:12.550 --> 00:45:14.653
you just have to have a desire to stop.

984
00:45:15.610 --> 00:45:18.380
And when you start to get it, your only obligation

985
00:45:18.380 --> 00:45:21.530
is you start paying it forward to other people.

986
00:45:21.530 --> 00:45:22.970
But do you have to bring a dollar,

987
00:45:22.970 --> 00:45:24.731
bring a dollar, bring a $1 bill.

988
00:45:24.731 --> 00:45:27.160
But if you don't have a dollar, ain't nothing but a thing,

989
00:45:27.160 --> 00:45:28.730
you have to have a dollar.

990
00:45:28.730 --> 00:45:30.057
You might feel weird if you're like,

991
00:45:30.057 --> 00:45:32.980
"Man, no one told me to bring (indistinct)."

992
00:45:32.980 --> 00:45:37.980
I mean, I just, I think it's one of the most miraculous

993
00:45:38.310 --> 00:45:41.830
things of modern times that it hasn't imploded either.

994
00:45:41.830 --> 00:45:43.340
Yeah, yeah.

995
00:45:43.340 --> 00:45:46.430
No, it's unbelievable, it's unbelievably miraculous.

996
00:45:46.430 --> 00:45:48.930
And I also love the like...

997
00:45:50.620 --> 00:45:53.690
I love the like secret handshake thing about it too,

998
00:45:53.690 --> 00:45:56.070
like that you meet people out in the wild

999
00:45:58.250 --> 00:46:00.490
like, it'll help you, like it'll help you.

1000
00:46:00.490 --> 00:46:02.810
And if you're in a new town, you can just pop in

1001
00:46:02.810 --> 00:46:06.280
and then you're instantly dialed into some...

1002
00:46:06.280 --> 00:46:08.393
You're instantly dialed into a community.

1003
00:46:12.839 --> 00:46:17.580
So I ran into an old friend in New York at a meeting

1004
00:46:17.580 --> 00:46:21.010
and he had been sober for awhile.

1005
00:46:21.010 --> 00:46:25.010
And we started going to this one meeting on Sundays

1006
00:46:25.010 --> 00:46:28.150
in the East Village, I can't remember the name of it now.

1007
00:46:28.150 --> 00:46:30.850
It was one of those big, like, not stadium,

1008
00:46:30.850 --> 00:46:34.510
but like the size of a big venue meeting

1009
00:46:34.510 --> 00:46:36.810
like it was in a playhouse or something.

1010
00:46:36.810 --> 00:46:38.670
And so they would do, 'cause it was once a week,

1011
00:46:38.670 --> 00:46:43.670
they would do like anniversary, like anyone with five years

1012
00:46:43.870 --> 00:46:47.220
and then there'd be a big line of people that would come up.

1013
00:46:47.220 --> 00:46:49.657
And this friend of mine pointed out, he said,

1014
00:46:49.657 --> 00:46:52.807
"Now watch between five years and 10 years,

1015
00:46:52.807 --> 00:46:54.670
"watch how few people go up."

1016
00:46:54.670 --> 00:46:57.957
So the person at the front, the meeting chair would be like,

1017
00:46:57.957 --> 00:47:00.650
"Okay, anybody with six years of sobriety."

1018
00:47:00.650 --> 00:47:03.350
And then like 11 people would come up.

1019
00:47:03.350 --> 00:47:06.600
Anyone with eight years of sobriety

1020
00:47:06.600 --> 00:47:07.990
and like three people would come up.

1021
00:47:07.990 --> 00:47:11.700
Anybody with one year of sobriety, line 40 people.

1022
00:47:11.700 --> 00:47:12.690
And he said, there's a...

1023
00:47:12.690 --> 00:47:14.587
He's like, "I went through it too and there's a trough

1024
00:47:14.587 --> 00:47:17.550
"between five and 10 years where you stop engaging."

1025
00:47:17.550 --> 00:47:19.180
